{"team":"CHI","col":"#F1873B","identity":"run-heavy","funnel":"run-funnel","plays_pg":64.3,"adot":8.5,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>Bleed the Clock</h2><p>The WR2 is unusually involved here \u2014 <strong>19%</strong> of targets (league ~15%), meaning there's bankable volume beyond the top receiver.</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>Their run game attacks the perimeter \u2014 <strong>31% of carries hit the edge</strong> (league ~25%), an outside-zone lean that rewards speed backs and can boom for chunk gains.</p><p>They're a heavy under-center team (61% shotgun vs ~68%) \u2014 a pro-style, run-committed structure.</p><p>When they fall behind they abandon the run entirely \u2014 58% pass while trailing, so their pass-catchers have huge comeback-script ceilings.</p><p>They play fast \u2014 <strong>64 snaps a game</strong> (league ~61), and the extra volume is a rising tide that lifts everyone's counting stats.</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Inside the 20 they lean run-heavy, passing <strong>52%</strong> of the time, funnelling touchdown equity to <strong>D'Andre Swift</strong>.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 The Run Comes Free</h2><p>They surrender <strong>134 rushing</strong> and <strong>239 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). The run moves against them \u2014 <strong>target opposing RB1s</strong>.</p><p>They give up deep shots (21% of throws travel 15+ vs ~19%) \u2014 big-play WR upside against them.</p><p>They leak <strong>RB rushing TDs</strong> (0.56/game vs ~0.46) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><p>They leak <strong>WR1 receiving TDs</strong> (0.47/game vs ~0.38) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: back <strong>D'Andre Swift</strong>'s rushing volume in favored/positive scripts; their pass-catchers have massive ceilings in comeback scripts (fade-material as underdogs); <strong>opposing RB1s</strong> smash on the ground and at the goal line.</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the pro